下面的代码会打印什么？为什么？

```js
for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 0);
}
```

1. 说出输出并解释原因，再给出至少两种让它依次打印 0、1、2 的改法。
2. 在代码框里实现 `once(fn)`：返回一个新函数，第一次调用时执行 `fn` 并记住返回值，之后的调用直接返回这个值，不再执行 `fn`。

What does this print, and why?

```js
for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 0);
}
```

1. Give the output and explain it, then show at least two ways to make it print 0, 1, 2.
2. In the code box, implement `once(fn)`: it returns a new function that runs `fn` on the first call and remembers its return value; later calls return that value without running `fn` again.

questions.solution:
Output: `3`, `3`, `3`. `var i` is a single binding for the whole function; the loop ends before any timer callback runs, so all three read `i === 3`.

Fixes: `for (let i = 0; ...)` (each iteration gets its own `i`); `setTimeout((j) => console.log(j), 0, i)`; or capture with an IIFE, `((j) => setTimeout(() => console.log(j), 0))(i)`.

```js
function once(fn) {
  let called = false;
  let result;
  return function (...args) {
    if (!called) {
      called = true;
      result = fn.apply(this, args);
    }
    return result;
  };
}
```

A flag rather than a `result === undefined` check, so a function returning `undefined` still runs once. Setting `called` before the call means a throwing `fn` is not retried; setting it after retries on the next call. Either is fine when the candidate states the choice.

